ext"},{"text":"Any of the following constant string values:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"standard"},{"text":": The legacy hillshade method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"basic"},{"text":": Basic hillshade. Uses a simple physics model where the reflected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light intensity is proportional to the cosine of the angle between the incident","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light and the surface normal. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gdaldem"},{"text":" default algorithm.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"combined"},{"type":"text","text":": Hillshade algorithm whose intensity scales with slope. Similar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to GDAL’s "},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"-combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" option."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"igor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Hillshade algorithm which tries to minimize effects on other map"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features beneath. Similar to GDAL’s "},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"-igor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" option."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"multidirectional","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Hillshade with multiple illumination directions. Uses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the basic hillshade model with multiple independent light sources."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Predefined functions, including mathematical and string operators"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Conditional expressions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Variable assignments and references to assigned variables"},{"type"